    "explanation": "This ruling is addressed to both of you, and I want to be straight about what this forum can and cannot do.\n\nTHE FARE (SGD 27.90). This was an upfront-quoted trip (RYDE_X, EV-FARE-00531). The quoted fare was SGD 27.90 and the amount charged on the platform was SGD 27.90, so charged_over_quote is 0.00 — nothing was added over the quote. The only other possible lines are the airport surcharge, recorded at SGD 0.00, and ERP/tolls, recorded at SGD 0.00. Under POL-RD-11 the distance and time charges are fixed at booking and no distance-or-time refund is available on an upfront-quoted trip, and there is no pass-through line to correct. The platform charge of SGD 27.90 is correct and stands.\n\nTHE ROUTE. The governing measurement is the GPS trace (EV-GPS-00531), which recorded 15.79 km against an optimal route of 15.50 km — an excess of 0.29 km, or 1.87%. That fails both POL-RD-01 tests (more than 0.8 km and more than 20%). The trace is complete (100% coverage, 10-second cadence, no gaps), so it is not impaired and no corroboration is needed. The absent traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00531-01 (weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT) therefore carries nothing, and no closure exoneration arises. No route deviation is established.\n\nTHE SGD 40. Ms Rider, the SGD 40 you describe is not ignored — it is recorded in the in-app chat (EV-CHAT-00531): the driver wrote 'airport surcharge cannot in app, paynow 40 pls' at 22:49:40 and you replied 'ok sent' at 22:50:40, and the driver's statement confirms he asked and was paid. So the payment is documented and I do not doubt you made it. The difficulty is remedy. The SGD 40 is not a line of the fare breakdown, and this tribunal's refund machinery runs only on fare-breakdown lines. POL-RD-09(4) refunds a charge line for a gantry the trace never crossed, or an airport surcharge on a trip that does NOT originate at an airport. This trip DID originate at Changi Terminal 2 (EV-TRIP-00531), and the ledger's surcharge line is SGD 0.00, so there is no wrongly applied surcharge line to refund — the SGD 40 was never a platform charge. No other clause in the loaded policy reaches a private transfer between the two of you, and POL-GEN-03 lets money move only as a fare refund or a platform payment to the driver. So the SGD 40 cannot be ordered returned in this forum, and I have not manufactured a referral to do it: a referral exists only where a clause produces one, and none does here (POL-RD-06(c) requires a material deviation and an established pattern, neither of which exists; POL-RD-09(4) requires a billing-integrity defect on the ledger, which does not exist).\n\nON ESCALATION. POL-RD-10 escalates only on its listed grounds. None is present: confidence is above 0.70; all identifiers match TRP-00531; the trace is unimpaired; the timestamps agree (started 22:51:40, ended 23:13:40 on both trip record and trace); no exculpatory clause is invoked against a missing artifact; any refund is zero, not above SGD 150 or the charged total; the evidence is consistent rather than two-sidedly contradictory; and every fare line has a counterpart. So this is not an escalation case, and the disputed sum is not held.\n\nWHAT I CAN SAY PLAINLY. The driver's in-app message that the airport surcharge 'cannot' go through the app does not match this platform's fare model, under which the airport surcharge is a platform line (SGD 6.00 off-peak / SGD 8.00 peak on a trip originating at Changi) and the platform charged none on this trip. The SGD 40 was collected off-platform and is outside what this fare-dispute process can order returned; if you wish to pursue it, that is a matter for the platform's trust-and-safety channel or between the two of you. On the money in this case, the outcome is NO_ACTION: the SGD 27.90 platform charge stands as charged and correct, and no refund or driver compensation issues."
