    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To both parties: this ruling deals with two separate things — the SGD 27.90 the platform charged for TRP-00531, and the separate SGD 40 the driver collected by PayNow.\n\nTHE FARE AND THE ROUTE ARE CLEAN. The fare ledger (EV-FARE-00531, weight 1.0) is an UPFRONT_QUOTE trip: the quoted fare of SGD 27.90 equals the charged total of SGD 27.90, so charged_over_quote is SGD 0.00. The airport_surcharge line is SGD 0.00, tolls_erp is SGD 0.00 and there are no ERP gantries. The GPS trace (EV-GPS-00531, weight 1.0) records 15.79 km driven against a 15.5 km optimal route — an excess of 0.29 km, or 1.87% — below both POL-RD-01 establishment gates (greater than 0.8 km AND greater than 20%). The rider's own claim that no distance was bought is correct: no route deviation exists, so POL-RD-01 directs NO_ACTION, and because the fare is upfront-quoted POL-RD-11 also closes the distance-and-time refund route (the charged total is not above the quote plus any properly chargeable pass-through). The rider's and driver's distance claims are accepted and agree.\n\nTHE SGD 40. The record does support the rider's account of what happened: the in-app chat (EV-CHAT-00531, weight 1.0) shows the driver writing 'airport surcharge cannot in app, paynow 40 pls' and the rider replying 'ok sent', and the driver's own counterparty statement confirms he asked for and received a payment. The rider is also right that the driver's premise was false: this policy's fare model makes the Changi airport surcharge a platform line (SGD 6.00 off-peak / SGD 8.00 peak) on a trip originating at Changi, not a cost 'the app doesn't cover'. But I cannot order the SGD 40 returned. The rider's POL-RD-09(4) argument is rejected: that limb reaches only (a) a charge line for a gantry the GPS trace never passes, or (b) an airport surcharge on a trip that does NOT originate at an airport. There are no gantry lines here, and this trip does originate at Changi Terminal 2, so a surcharge would be properly chargeable — and in any event the ledger carries no surcharge line at all. The SGD 40 is not a fare_breakdown line; it is a private transfer between the parties, and POL-RD-09 corrects fare lines, not off-platform payments. POL-RD-11, POL-RD-09 and POL-GEN-03 move money only as a fare refund to the filing party, a pass-through correction, or a platform/fee-funded payment to the driver. No clause in the loaded policy licenses an order to return an off-platform payment, so nothing is refundable on this record and no compensation is due to the driver either (there is no unbilled distance — the billed 15.8 km is not short of the trace).\n\nTHE ESCALATION ARGUMENT (rider) is rejected. POL-RD-10 lists its triggers and none fires: trip identifiers match across trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown (trigger 2 no); the trace is COMPLETE at 100% coverage, no gaps, 10 s cadence, so it is not impaired under POL-RD-07(a)-(c) (trigger 3 no); timestamps are consistent (trigger 4 no); no exculpatory clause was invoked against a missing artifact — the driver never asserted a closure, a rider-requested detour or a relocation (trigger 5 no); the refund does not approach the ceilings (trigger 6 no); there is no comparably strong contradictory evidence (trigger 7 no); every fare line has a counterpart (trigger 8 no); and confidence is above the 0.70 floor (trigger 1 no). Nor is the SGD 40 'a sum the record cannot carry' — the chat log and the driver's statement carry it. The missing traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00531-01 (weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT) is noted, but the driver invoked no road-closure excuse, so its absence decides nothing and it carries no finding.\n\nCONFIDENCE. Every artifact carrying the deciding facts — the fare ledger, the GPS trace and the chat log — is at weight 1.0, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0; the bundle mean is context only. Confidence is set at 0.90.\n\nOUTCOME. No clause provides a monetary remedy, so the outcome is NO_ACTION. The SGD 27.90 charge stands as charged, and no refund or driver compensation issues. The SGD 40 is an off-platform payment outside this forum; nothing in this ruling prevents the rider from raising the driver's off-app surcharge demand with the platform's off-platform-payment or fraud process, and that remains the proper route for it."
